      "source": [
        {
          "question": "q-48700",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The instantaneous rate of change in the spread when $t=9$ days is equal to ${f}^{\u2032}(9).$ \n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{100\\,({t}^{3}+2)}{t+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{100(3{t}^{2})(t+1)-100({t}^{3}+2)(1)}{{(t+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =100\\cdot \\frac{2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-2}{{(t+1)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=9,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(9) & =100\\cdot \\frac{2(9)^{3}+3(9)^{2}-2}{{((9)+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =100\\cdot \\frac{1\\,458+243-2}{100} \\\\  & =1\\,699.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change in the spread when $t=9$ is $1\\,699$ computers per day.",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "d4e5a48a7258fe67eaecb883db90efba2089bb6b04e5d48438a775866113552b"
        }
      ],
