    {
      "question": "e-6174",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/problem",
      "old_sha256": "086f46c4deb9c32b6fd5ff38c7eb9b95aca2b6ae05ab8a20aeaa936af03bbbae",
      "new_sha256": "9a9520ce4433e9457622a05b6945bd9741facd7be7957adfaad404c3800e2513",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-6174",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "A particle moves in a straight line. After $t$ seconds the particle is $\\, f(t)=2t^3 - 5t + 9\\,$ feet away from its initial position. What is the instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position as a function of $t?$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/example-6174.json",
          "file_sha256": "43b4da3c29d66e41ab73e182f8b8a6499e6837ece13aa3c8243afeaab747e141"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1279,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 1280
    },
    {
      "question": "e-6174",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "4400d9938f86f91c850b31ae348b8643ffc25beff2d5a50f13feb24983c776c7",
      "new_sha256": "40fa6f4ee293b635a9169df0b58e771b8436bd8ad78afc03fb86394b9af890ec",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-6174",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position is equal to $f'(t).$ \n\nWe take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-5t+9) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t$ seconds, the instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position is $6t^2 - 5$ feet per second.",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/example-6174.json",
          "file_sha256": "43b4da3c29d66e41ab73e182f8b8a6499e6837ece13aa3c8243afeaab747e141"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1279,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 1280
    },
    {
      "question": "e-276",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/problem",
      "old_sha256": "ac4d13a9069fd55e6b79c1e4110f53042105acfa3caace167991a7b2888d887a",
      "new_sha256": "0c017e31adbe92c240f56d4d40cc20f88efd6173b810f8a8ea8b4c17ffbd03cd",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-276",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Lizzie buys $b$ pounds of bananas at a price $p,$ in dollars, that can be modeled by the function $p(b)=5e^{-0.2b}.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of the price when $b=5$ pounds?",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/example-276.json",
          "file_sha256": "6b4d7993b87fec8a4f3f14cfc7679a9eada9f561d46a9540e92d306856bbcddd"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1279,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 1280
    },
    {
      "question": "e-276",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "6c83a58594b0b173f179ec611fba36e165ee5e59e6ebdd255b959089820273ec",
      "new_sha256": "ed3df199c5d12be384252e7281c7737a5234487cdcb501614e40403cd591d144",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-276",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The instantaneous rate of change of the price when $b=5$ pounds is equal to $p'(5).$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{\u2032}(b) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(5{e}^{-0.2b}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{-0.2b}\\cdot (-0.2) \\\\  & =-{e}^{-0.2b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $b=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{\u2032}(5) & =-{e}^{-0.2(5)} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the price when $b=5$ pounds is $-\\dfrac{1}{e}$ dollars per pound.",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/example-276.json",
          "file_sha256": "6b4d7993b87fec8a4f3f14cfc7679a9eada9f561d46a9540e92d306856bbcddd"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1279,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 1280
    },
    {
      "question": "e-275",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/problem",
      "old_sha256": "f7a610cdb4e57ed680b07f0301b8dd398e9f42dfc886d097ff00536d4f08dbf2",
      "new_sha256": "65cfed95095ff607b7066b3815b679aca83f61aee15dd1d0208434e4b1be4ff1",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-275",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "A spherical balloon is being inflated so that its volume is increasing. Find the instantaneous rate at which the volume of the balloon is changing with respect to the radius at the moment when the diameter of the balloon is equal to $12\\, \\text{cm}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/assets/e03fb046f74771676d7b1e83a1cf09176adcffaf8112e9de263404b8be74b026.png)",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/example-275.json",
          "file_sha256": "f594050fdb6305e0ff11c07ed32a43a8f17fa20c3a0592ef1eab3dd76906792c"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1279,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 1280
    },
    {
      "question": "e-275",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "6f8fb52db80448f25ea35bbf53a42a86dd2aa42cf7a0b9218a18711f7b7bb14b",
      "new_sha256": "be48e29c6f0de6f84d8febd1544c3fe62eb88405fa540561a86b0828a5f25736",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-275",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Since we are given that the diameter of the balloon is $12\\, \\text{cm},$ its radius is $r =6\\, \\text{cm}.$ Now, we know that the volume of a sphere with radius $r$  is given by \n\n$$\nV= V(r) = \\dfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^3.\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $V(r)$  with respect to $r$ is \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\nV'(r) &= \\dfrac{\\textrm d }{\\textrm d r}\\left(  \\dfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\\right)\\[5pt]\n &  =  \\dfrac{4}{3}\\pi (3r^2)\\[5pt]\n &= 4\\pi r^2, \n}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $r=6$ gives\n\n$$\nV'(6)=  4\\pi (6)^2= 144\\pi.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the volume of the balloon is changing when its diameter is $12\\, \\text{cm}\\,$ is $\\, 144\\pi \\, \\text{cm}^3/\\text{cm}.$\n\n**Note:** We read $\\text{cm}^3/\\text{cm}$ as \"centimeters cubed per centimeter\".",
